Z||000017||c m west||06-14-2001||10:41 PM||||unfortunatley Hollywood has gotten a hold of the San Fernando racing scene ( Silmar, Tampa, Sun Valley, Roxford, etc. ) I grew up around the racing scene with all of my friends, I remember about 10 years ago when it was solidly Mustangs vs. Camaros. Now it has grown into Neon lighted, nitrous injected, Soy Sauce Burning econo boxes, I have nothing against imports, this is simply how I myslef refer to them.<P> Now before anyone goes jumping into conclusions, yes,  I have been a street racer for several years and will continue to do so for years to come. Meeting up at street racing solicits alot of buisness for me ( Imprezza Turbos, Mustangs, Camaros, street trucks ) and is very safe under the right conditions.<P> However what ruins it all is when it gets blown out of proportion, re-discovered by the media, gang and culture involved, and exploited by those who do not belong there.<P> Street racing has been around since the advent of the automobile and will still continue to do so far after were all gone, so it is not a phase or a fad, either get out there and have fun, or just avoid the places where they meet up.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>1991 Twin Turbo Chevy K5 Blazer 4x4<BR>1996 3.4 DOHC Turbo Fiero GT Coupe<BR>1999 Subaru Imprezza RS 2.5 Turbo<P>||||reg||1
